  ('754b2ad0-5344-5a74-afa2-d52f0344edcd', 'en-ak5-meningar-1', 'Engelska', 'ak5', 'Meningar', 'Frågor med do och does', 'Hur man bygger frågor med do och does.', 10, 'vanlig', null),
  ('22e2d40f-6794-50a5-956a-539e3812276f', 'en-ak5-meningar-2', 'Engelska', 'ak5', 'Meningar', 'Don''t och doesn''t', 'Att säga att något inte är så, med not, don''t och doesn''t.', 11, 'vanlig', null),
  ('b6689939-620f-543d-b8e1-b1150e1a7d58', 'en-ak5-mastare-meningar', 'Engelska', 'ak5', 'Meningar', 'Mästarprov: Meningar', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 12, 'mastare', null),
  ('eb3d9aed-37a7-5502-ac62-68f76b201cfb', 'en-ak5-lasforstaelse-1', 'Engelska', 'ak5', 'Läsförståelse', 'A new girl', 'En berättelse om en ny flicka i klassen, med frågor om vad som står.', 13, 'vanlig', 'Today a new girl started in our class. Her name is Lily, and she comes from Canada. She has long red hair and a big smile.

Our teacher, Mr Brown, asked me to show Lily the school. First we went to the library. Lily loves books, and she found a book about horses. Then we went to the dining hall. We had fish and potatoes for lunch. Lily does not eat fish, so she only ate potatoes and salad.

After lunch we played football in the schoolyard. Lily is very good at football! She scored two goals.

When school ended, Lily''s dad picked her up. She waved and said, “See you tomorrow!” I think we are going to be friends.'),
  ('244cfb28-ef73-58a0-b4e6-b3ccec4c7dc7', 'en-ak5-lasforstaelse-2', 'Engelska', 'ak5', 'Läsförståelse', 'Lost cat', 'En lapp om en borttappad katt, med frågor om vad som står.', 14, 'vanlig', 'LOST CAT

Have you seen Tiger? Tiger is our cat. She is three years old. She is grey with white paws and a long tail. She wears a blue collar with a little bell.

Tiger went missing on Monday evening from our house on Park Road. She is a friendly cat, but she is afraid of dogs, so she may be hiding in a garden or under a car.

Tiger needs her medicine every morning.

If you see her, please do not try to catch her. Knock on our door at 12 Park Road and we will come at once.

We miss her very much. Thank you!

Emma and family, 12 Park Road'),
